{"id": "unknown-2026-11-26-017", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["panel_price", "oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Omdia: sales of OLED displays with active privacy view to reach over 90 million units in 2033", "content": "<p>Market research firm Omdia forecasts that shipments of OLED displays with Active Privacy View (APV) technology - displays that can narrow their viewing angle on demand so that the screen cannot be seen by people nearby - will reach 91.7 million units in 2033, or around 6.6% of all OLED display shipments that year. In 2026, APV OLED shipments are expected to reach 16.5 million units, driven by the first adoptions in smartphones and laptops.</p><img class=\"align-center align-center\" src=\"https:", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/omdia-oled-displays-active-privacy-view-reach-917-million-units-2033", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "boe-2026-11-26-018", "date": "2026-11-26", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 48, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": ["boe"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Why is BOE interested in Visionox?", "content": "<p>We recently reported that <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/boe-reportedly-talks-acquire-visionox\">BOE is reportedly in talks to acquire Visionox</a>. The talks started with a single production line, and have since expanded to a possible takeover of the entire company. Visionox is in a difficult financial position - but it is also, arguably, the most technically ambitious OLED maker in China. In this article we look at what BOE stands to gain from such a deal, and why it makes sense for Chin", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/why-boe-interested-visionox", "type": "rss"}]}
